  "worked_solution": "By Newton\u2019s second law,\n\n$$\nF(t)=ma(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $F(t)$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a(t)$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+t\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force, in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =ma(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t-t\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
